    <!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
    <string name="faq_title">FAQ</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">How Do I Save A Status?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Grant folder access once, then tap the download button on any image or video. Saved files go to Pictures/WAVAULT and Movies/WAVAULT and appear in your gallery.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">Does It Work With WhatsApp Business?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">Yes. WAVAULT shows statuses from WhatsApp and WhatsApp Business together. No switching needed.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">How Are New Statuses Detected?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">WAVAULT checks every few seconds while open and every 15 minutes in the background, and notifies you when a new status file appears. Keep New Status Alerts on in Settings.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Why Is A Status Missing?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">WAVAULT can only show statuses that WhatsApp has already downloaded to your phone. WhatsApp often downloads them in the background, especially on Wi-Fi. If one is missing, open WhatsApp once and it will appear here automatically.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">Will The Person Know I Saved It?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">No. WAVAULT only reads files on your phone. It never contacts WhatsApp or sends anything.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">Why Is Folder Access Needed?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">Android protects WhatsApp media files. You allow access once and WAVAULT reads only status files.</string>
    <string name="faq_q7">Why Do Statuses Disappear?</string>
    <string name="faq_a7">WhatsApp deletes statuses after 24 hours. Save them, or turn on Auto-Save in Settings.</string>
    <string name="faq_q8">Can I Edit Before Reposting?</string>
    <string name="faq_a8">Yes. Open a status, tap Edit, and crop, add filters, text or drawing, or trim videos. The original file is never changed.</string>

